## 4. TEST PROTOCOLS (LOCKED, NOT EXECUTED - no articles exist)
Metrology chain (all register tests): mass x3 median, balance
0.1 g class or better (mass +-0.1%); volume by TWO methods with
the 1.0% accord rule (disagreement = METROLOGY INVALID, never a
design kill); blind seat computation, expected seats hidden until
splits are written; raw-readings rule - a verdict without raw
readings does not exist. Seat sigma 0.00128 nats (D-GS3-class
budget); PASS bar 3 sigma = 0.00384 nats.
T-UUC1 REGISTER TEST (P1-A): blind weigh/measure; PASS if the
measured split seats within 3 sigma of 18.2113 AND E within its
3-sigma band of 87.7150. KILL: seat outside the shell
[17.7192, 18.671974] - the article is not the designed article.
T-UUC2 INGEST TEST: replay the EQS-1051 feeds (Gaia slice sha
4888a3ab..., GOES day file) through the article; PASS if the census
seats at E 213.3187 within the run's own tolerance and every sample
count accords (1,200 / 1,434). KILL: any fitted parameter appearing
in the article's chain - the chain is computed, never fitted.
T-UUC3 CLOCK TEST: checksum evaluated at z 0 / 10.6 / 14.44 / 1100
on the article; PASS if Kd_U x T-dagger holds 2.697836e-29 K within
1e-12 relative at all four stations. KILL: any station off.
T-UUC4 CRYPTO TEST: 100 records encrypted and decrypted through
the article's module; PASS = byte-exact round trip 100/100 (the
EQS record standard). KILL: any mismatch.
T-UUC5 PHOTONIC TEST (P1-B): calibrated source at six flux levels
(decades 4-9 centres: 4.304e+01, 4.304e+02, 4.304e+03, 4.304e+04, 4.304e+05, 4.304e+06 W/m2);
PASS if the head's priced flux accords with the calibrated setting
within 1% at all six levels AND the aperture income at the D5
level accords with the cross-section law within 1%. KILL: any
level off by more than 1%, or any verdict issued for a level the
source did not set (a phantom detection).

